  "$comment": "Port-level wiring between the Frontend's blocks, declared as data. No integrated top-level exists in the RTL drop, so the validation subsystem generates its own integration harness (chain_harness_gen.py) from this map. Every connection is checkable against the manifests: named ports must exist and widths must agree \u2014 a rename or resize in a regenerated drop becomes a loud structural failure, not a silently unconnected net.",
  "$provenance": "Derived by reading the block manifests side by side (catalog v1.15 streams give the intent; the manifests give the port names). Where the blocks' interfaces do not actually compose, the gap is recorded in `glue` with a filed finding rather than silently papered over.",
